Game of Life of benchmarks/life on the machine's GPU, on
small grids: the cells are right (life.test), each kernel is an SPMD
kernel, and the arrays stay on the device for the steps.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life.m -o %t2
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=16 LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t2 2> %t.info | FileCheck %s
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=INFO < %t.info
CHECK: Population: 9339
CHECK-NEXT: Checksum: 429141631
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 LIFE_SOUP=100 %t2 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SOUP
SOUP: Soup: 100 x 100 cells at the centre
SOUP-NEXT: Population: 1133
SOUP-NEXT: Checksum: 51448204
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}life.init_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO: Launching kernel {{.*}}life.step_{{.*}} in SPMD mode
INFO-NOT: Generic

After the region's copies to the device, no step copies either array, until
the region copies them back: 302 x 302 cells of 8 bytes and the array's
size are 729640 bytes.
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIBOMPTARGET_INFO=32 LIFE_SIZE=300 LIFE_STEPS=25 %t2 2> %t.copies > /dev/null
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=COPIES < %t.copies
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=A, at {{.*}}life.m:[[REGION:[0-9]+]]:
COPIES: Copying data from host to device, {{.*}}Name=B, at {{.*}}life.m:[[REGION]]:
COPIES-NOT: Size=729640
COPIES: Copying data from device to host, {{.*}}Size=729640, {{.*}}life.m:[[REGION]]:
